'' T26, RUN: 'mid( u, start[, len] ) = x' over a USTRING overwrites in place, as fbc-modern
'' does: fb_UStrAssignMid with the source converted to UTF-16 -- a literal, a string, a
'' zstring, a wstring, a concatenation, a function's string result -- and over a
'' 'ustring * N' through its buffer and tagged length. tiko declined every source but a
'' ustring and dropped the statement with nothing said. The other direction too: a
'' ustring source into a string or zstring is converted to narrow (fb_UStrToStr), where
'' its UTF-16 bytes were written as narrow text, and into a wstring it passes its data
'' pointer, where it was dropped. Output byte-identical to fbc-modern's.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/mid-stmt-ustring.bas -o tests/codegen/midstmtustring.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/codegen/midstmtustring.exe
'' RUN: tests/codegen/midstmtustring.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: aXYZefgh
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: aXYZefQR
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 1XYZefQR
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: hÉLLÖ wörld 11
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: aab
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: WWxy##gh
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: WWxy##gL 8
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  4 88
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 1zz456
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: aÄÖf
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: abÄÖ
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  619699
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: aZZdef
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: aZZÄÖf
